# Third-party and derived material

This repository contains material that is not original work. This file records
where it came from and under what terms.

## 1. Vendored from `jhaizhou-ops/d2r-mobile`

`vendor/d2r-mobile/` is a copy of a subset of
<https://github.com/jhaizhou-ops/d2r-mobile>, pinned to commit
`9de307ecaff42b3c9d45e58992c848ee89b8f6a1` (2026-10-15). See
`vendor/MANIFEST.tsv` for a per-file SHA-256 record.

- Upstream project licence: **MIT**, Copyright (c) 2026 jhaizhou.
- The vendored files are unmodified; the file list is in
  `docs/MIGRATION-1.md`.
- The MIT notice for these files is the upstream one; this repository's own
  `LICENSE` covers the adapter code written here.

### 1a. A note on the offline-play patch rules

Upstream's `dm/tools/patch_nso.py` contains seven rewrite rules that exist so the
game can run without a network connection, and upstream states plainly that
**those seven rules are taken from an existing community offline fix (LFS Mod
Offline Fix), not their own work**, and that they have no reliable record of
where it was first published or who wrote it. That statement applies equally to
the copy vendored here.

If you are the author of that fix, please open an issue and you will be credited.

